// Prolog 4 — structure and recursion: circuits
//
// The classic Prolog circuits lesson, inverted: instead of nested
// terms DESCRIBING an invisible circuit, we build a visible one and
// let the facts fall out of geometry. Contact is a fact the scene
// derives — press the facts button and find touches(blade_s, wire_s2,
// 0, 2.21): two conductors, in contact, with a time interval.
//
// The rules layer defines conductivity as RECURSION over contact
// (see rules.pl):
//   reaches(A, B, T) :- ...touches_at(A, B, T)... or a chain of them
// One rule, any circuit. Series and parallel are not term structure
// here — they are LAYOUT. Look at the scene: the series circuit is
// one chain; the parallel circuit is two visible paths.

time closed 1
time opened 4

// ---- the SERIES circuit (north lane): one path, one point of failure
set circuit_s battery_s wire_s1 blade_s wire_s2 bulb_s
box battery_s size(0.6 0.6 0.6) at(0.3 0.3 2) color(#c0392b)
box wire_s1 size(1 0.1 0.2) at(1.1 0.05 2) color(#7f8c8d)
box blade_s size(0.8 0.1 0.2) at(2 0.05 2) color(#b8860b)
box wire_s2 size(1 0.1 0.2) at(2.9 0.05 2) color(#7f8c8d)
sphere bulb_s r(0.25) at(3.65 0.25 2) color(#f4d03f)

// ---- the PARALLEL circuit (south lane): two paths share the load
set circuit_p battery_p junction wire_p blade_p collector bulb_p
box battery_p size(0.6 0.6 0.6) at(0.3 0.3 -2) color(#c0392b)
box junction size(0.2 0.2 1.8) at(0.7 0.1 -2) color(#7f8c8d)
box wire_p size(1.4 0.1 0.2) at(1.5 0.05 -1.2) color(#7f8c8d)
box blade_p size(1.4 0.1 0.2) at(1.5 0.05 -2.8) color(#b8860b)
box collector size(0.2 0.2 1.8) at(2.3 0.1 -2) color(#7f8c8d)
sphere bulb_p r(0.25) at(2.65 0.25 -2) color(#f4d03f)

// at t=2 both switch blades swing open — 90° up, a real physical gap
turn blade_s to(0 0 90) over(0.5) start(2)
turn blade_p to(0 0 90) over(0.5) start(2)
// the series bulb dies with its only path; the paint is the author
// AGREEING with the engine (see the reaches goals below) — color is
// projection, the derivation is the fact
paint bulb_s to(#4a4a42) start(2.5)

// ---- the LIVE layer: these follow the scrubber — drag it
? touches(blade_s wire_s2)
? when touches(blade_s wire_s2)
check ever touches(blade_s wire_s2)
check never touches(blade_s wire_s2) during(3 4)

// ---- the RULES layer: recursion over contact facts, time explicit.
// Variables unify across the chain: reaches walks touches_at links
// the way Prolog walks any relation — this is the same machinery as
// could_be_at and testimony, pointed at electricity.
?- reaches(battery_s, bulb_s, closed)
?- reaches(battery_s, bulb_s, opened)
?- reaches(battery_p, bulb_p, opened)
?- reaches_set(battery_p, opened, Xs)

// series: lit, then dead. parallel: lit BOTH times — one branch broke,
// the other carried it. No clause says "parallel is redundant";
// redundancy is derived from the shape of the world.

// ---- the same circuit, unplugged --------------------------------------
// In pure Prolog you would write the structure as nested terms and
// teach unification against them — no world, no time, no gap to see:
//
//   conducts(wire).
//   conducts(switch(closed)).          % no clause for switch(open)
//   conducts(series(A, B))   :- conducts(A), conducts(B).
//   conducts(parallel(A, _)) :- conducts(A).
//   conducts(parallel(_, B)) :- conducts(B).
//
// Same lesson, no body. Here the structure is the scene, the terms
// are facts derived from geometry, and "when is it lit" is a question
// the pure version cannot even ask.
